--- !u!114 &2080022344
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2080022341}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c95e78bf911a63f44883f1c567c65a49, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  bancoDePreguntas:
  - nombreDificultad: "Muy f\xE1cil"
    preguntas:
    - informacionComplementaria: Paris is the capital and largest city of France.
        It is known for landmarks such as the Eiffel Tower and the Louvre Museum.
      enunciado: What is the capital of France?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Rome
      - texto: Paris
      - texto: Madrid
      - texto: Berlin
      respuestaCorrecta: 1
    - informacionComplementaria: Water is made of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen
        atom, which is why its formula is H2O.
      enunciado: What is the chemical formula for water?
      respuestas:
      - texto: O2
      - texto: CO2
      - texto: H2O
      - texto: NaCl
      respuestaCorrecta: 2
    - informacionComplementaria: The blue whale is the largest mammal and the largest
        animal known to have ever existed on Earth.
      enunciado: Which animal is the largest mammal in the world?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Elephant
      - texto: Giraffe
      - texto: Hippopotamus
      - texto: Blue Whale
      respuestaCorrecta: 3
    - informacionComplementaria: Tokyo is the capital of Japan and one of the largest
        metropolitan areas in the world.
      enunciado: What is the capital of Japan?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Kyoto
      - texto: Tokyo
      - texto: Osaka
      - texto: Nagoya
      respuestaCorrecta: 1
    - informacionComplementaria: Humans need oxygen for cellular respiration, the
        process that releases energy from food.
      enunciado: Which gas do humans need to breathe?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Oxygen
      - texto: Nitrogen
      - texto: Helium
      - texto: Hydrogen
      respuestaCorrecta: 0
  - nombreDificultad: "F\xE1cil"
    preguntas:
    - informacionComplementaria: Au is the chemical symbol for gold and comes from
        the Latin word 'Aurum'.
      enunciado: Which element has the chemical symbol Au?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Silver
      - texto: Aluminum
      - texto: Gold
      - texto: Argon
      respuestaCorrecta: 2
    - informacionComplementaria: The heart pumps blood through the circulatory system
        to all parts of the body.
      enunciado: Which organ pumps blood throughout the human body?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Lungs
      - texto: Kidneys
      - texto: Liver
      - texto: Heart
      respuestaCorrecta: 3
    - informacionComplementaria: Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius under normal
        atmospheric pressure.
      enunciado: At what temperature does water boil at sea level?
      respuestas:
      - texto: "90\xB0C"
      - texto: "95\xB0C"
      - texto: "100\xB0C"
      - texto: "110\xB0C"
      respuestaCorrecta: 2
    - informacionComplementaria: The Titanic sank during its first voyage after striking
        an iceberg.
      enunciado: Which famous ship sank after hitting an iceberg in 1912?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Britannic
      - texto: Titanic
      - texto: Lusitania
      - texto: Queen Mary
      respuestaCorrecta: 1
    - informacionComplementaria: Vincent van Gogh painted The Starry Night in 1889.
      enunciado: Who painted The Starry Night?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Vincent van Gogh
      - texto: Pablo Picasso
      - texto: "Salvador Dal\xED"
      - texto: Claude Monet
      respuestaCorrecta: 0
  - nombreDificultad: Normal
    preguntas:
    - informacionComplementaria: France gifted the Statue of Liberty to the United
        States in 1886.
      enunciado: Which country gifted the Statue of Liberty to the United States?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Germany
      - texto: Italy
      - texto: Spain
      - texto: France
      respuestaCorrecta: 3
    - informacionComplementaria: Albert Einstein introduced the theory of relativity
        in the early 20th century.
      enunciado: Which scientist developed the theory of relativity?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Albert Einstein
      - texto: Isaac Newton
      - texto: Galileo Galilei
      - texto: Niels Bohr
      respuestaCorrecta: 0
    - informacionComplementaria: Michelangelo painted the famous ceiling of the Sistine
        Chapel in Vatican City.
      enunciado: Who painted the ceiling of the Sistine Chapel?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Leonardo da Vinci
      - texto: Raphael
      - texto: Michelangelo
      - texto: Donatello
      respuestaCorrecta: 2
    - informacionComplementaria: The Pacific Ocean contains the Mariana Trench, the
        deepest known point on Earth.
      enunciado: Which ocean is the deepest?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Atlantic Ocean
      - texto: Arctic Ocean
      - texto: Pacific Ocean
      - texto: Indian Ocean
      respuestaCorrecta: 2
    - informacionComplementaria: WWW stands for World Wide Web, the system of linked
        pages on the internet.
      enunciado: What does WWW stand for?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Web World Wide
      - texto: Wide World Web
      - texto: World Web Wide
      - texto: World Wide Web
      respuestaCorrecta: 3
  - nombreDificultad: "Dif\xEDcil"
    preguntas:
    - informacionComplementaria: The Odyssey is an ancient Greek epic poem traditionally
        attributed to Homer.
      enunciado: Who wrote 'The Odyssey'?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Plato
      - texto: Homer
      - texto: Sophocles
      - texto: Virgil
      respuestaCorrecta: 1
    - informacionComplementaria: The Berlin Wall fell in 1989, marking the beginning
        of German reunification.
      enunciado: In which year did the Berlin Wall fall?
      respuestas:
      - texto: 1989
      - texto: 1988
      - texto: 1991
      - texto: 1979
      respuestaCorrecta: 0
    - informacionComplementaria: Nicolaus Copernicus proposed that the planets orbit
        the Sun.
      enunciado: Who developed the heliocentric model of the Solar System?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Galileo
      - texto: Kepler
      - texto: Tycho Brahe
      - texto: Copernicus
      respuestaCorrecta: 3
    - informacionComplementaria: An octopus has three hearts that help circulate
        blood through its body.
      enunciado: How many hearts does an octopus have?
      respuestas:
      - texto: 1
      - texto: 3
      - texto: 2
      - texto: 4
      respuestaCorrecta: 1
    - informacionComplementaria: Sudan has more pyramids than Egypt, most of them
        built by the Kingdom of Kush.
      enunciado: Which country has the most pyramids in the world?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Peru
      - texto: Sudan
      - texto: Mexico
      - texto: Egypt
      respuestaCorrecta: 1
  - nombreDificultad: "Muy dif\xEDcil"
    preguntas:
    - informacionComplementaria: The first YouTube video was 'Me at the Zoo', uploaded
        in 2005.
      enunciado: What was the first video uploaded to YouTube called?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Hello World
      - texto: My First Video
      - texto: Me at the Zoo
      - texto: At the Zoo
      respuestaCorrecta: 2
    - informacionComplementaria: The Mona Lisa was stolen in 1911 and recovered two
        years later.
      enunciado: Which famous painting was stolen from the Louvre in 1911?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Mona Lisa
      - texto: The Scream
      - texto: The Last Supper
      - texto: Girl with a Pearl Earring
      respuestaCorrecta: 0
    - informacionComplementaria: Ganymede is the largest moon in the Solar System.
      enunciado: What is the name of the largest moon of Jupiter?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Europa
      - texto: Io
      - texto: Ganymede
      - texto: Callisto
      respuestaCorrecta: 2
    - informacionComplementaria: HTML is the standard markup language used to create
        web pages.
      enunciado: What does 'HTML' stand for?
      respuestas:
      - texto: HighText Machine Language
      - texto: HyperText Markup Language
      - texto: Hyper Transfer Markup Language
      - texto: Home Tool Markup Language
      respuestaCorrecta: 1
    - informacionComplementaria: The Volga River is the longest river in Europe.
      enunciado: What is the name of the longest river in Europe?
      respuestas:
      - texto: Dnieper
      - texto: Danube
      - texto: Rhine
      - texto: Volga
      respuestaCorrecta: 3
  enunciado: {fileID: 674629002}
  respuesta:
  - {fileID: 1482403052}
  - {fileID: 548600087}
  - {fileID: 1270774988}
